        "input": "This is a task from an agent benchmark. Can you return the `mapped_rxn` associated with the template that, when applied to the molecule below (provided as available input data), reproduces the reaction: The Still-Gennari reaction is a modification of the Horner-Wadsworth-Emmons (HWE) reaction that allows for the selective formation of (Z)-alkenes from aldehydes and phosphonate esters. The reaction typically involves the use of a phosphonate ester with electron-withdrawing groups, such as bis(trifluoroethyl) or bis(2,2,2-trifluoroethyl) groups, which helps to stabilize the carbanion intermediate formed during the reaction. Thus, a carbon-carbon double bond and a carbon-oxygen bond are formed, while a carbon-phosphorus bond, a carbon-carbon bond, and a carbon-oxygen bond are broken. Additionally, the triple bond of an alkyne is changed to a single bond. As a result, 'C-C double bonds' and  'carboxylic esters' functional groups are formed.\n\nBelow are a few scenarios that may contain an agent's correct/incorrect thought-action pairs.\n\nWhich scenario corresponds to a correct/incorrect tought-action pair?",
        "target_scores": {
          "<thought>\nLet me analyze the task:\n\n1. I need to find a template that, when applied to a molecule, reproduces the Still-Gennari reaction (a retrosynthetic step)\n2. The Still-Gennari reaction is described as forming C-C double bonds and carboxylic esters\n3. In the forward reaction: C-C double bond and C-O bond are formed, while C-P bond, C-C bond, and C-O bond are broken\n4. An alkyne triple bond changes to a single bond\n5. I have available input data showing precursors from a previous task\n\nFrom the available input data, I can see the product molecule is:\n'CCOC(=O)C[C@H]1C[C@H](O)[C@@H](C)[C@@H](/C=C(/C)C(=O)OC)O1'\n\nThis molecule has a C=C double bond and carboxylic ester groups, which matches the Still-Gennari reaction products.\n\nSince this is a retrosynthetic step, I need to find a template that breaks down this product. The hint describes the forward reaction, so in retrosynthesis:\n- C-C double bonds and carboxylic esters would be broken/modified\n- C-P bonds would be formed\n- The reaction involves phosphonate esters\n\nLet me search for templates that match these criteria. I'll search for templates that:\n- Break C-C double bonds (bonds_broken in forward = bonds_formed in retro)\n- Involve the target molecule\n- Form C-P bonds (in retrosynthesis, what's broken in forward is formed in retro)\n\nLet me start by searching the template catalog with the appropriate criteria.\n</thought>\n\n<action>search_template_catalog_by_criteria</action>\n<action_input>\n{\n  \"molecule_smiles\": \"CCOC(=O)C[C@H]1C[C@H](O)[C@@H](C)[C@@H](/C=C(/C)C(=O)OC)O1\",\n  \"functional_groups_formed\": [\"C-C double bonds\", \"carboxylic esters\"],\n  \"bonds_formed\": [\"6-6\", \"6-8\"],\n  \"bonds_broken\": [\"6-15\", \"6-6\", \"6-8\"],\n  \"limit\": 20\n}\n</action_input>": 1.0,
          "<thought>\nLet me analyze this task step by step:\n\n1. I need to find a template that, when applied to a molecule, reproduces the Still-Gennari reaction (a retrosynthetic step)\n2. The Still-Gennari reaction is described as forming:\n   - C-C double bonds\n   - Carboxylic esters\n   And breaking:\n   - C-P bonds\n   - C-C bonds\n   - C-O bonds\n   And changing alkyne triple bonds to single bonds\n\n3. I have available input data showing precursors from a previous task (make_5_lvl2-apply_template-4), which gives me three possible precursor molecules.\n\n4. Since the task mentions \"the molecule below (provided as available input data)\", I need to identify the target molecule. Looking at the precursors, they all seem to be variations of a similar structure with protecting groups and different positions of mesylate (OS(C)(=O)=O) and silyl protecting groups.\n\nLet me first understand what molecule I'm working with. The precursors suggest the target molecule should be the product after applying a template. Since this is a retrosynthetic task and I need to find the template that reproduces the Still-Gennari reaction, I should:\n\n1. First, identify the target molecule (the product of the Still-Gennari reaction)\n2. Search for templates that match the Still-Gennari reaction criteria\n3. Verify which template produces the given precursors\n\nLet me start by searching for templates with the criteria described for the Still-Gennari reaction. Since we're doing retrosynthesis, the forward reaction forms C-C double bonds and carboxylic esters, so in retrosynthesis these would be broken.\n\nLet me search for templates matching the Still-Gennari reaction criteria.\n</thought>\n\n<action>search_template_catalog_by_criteria</action>\n<action_input>\n{\n  \"molecule_smiles\": \"CC(C)(C)OC(=O)N1[C@@H](C[C@@H](CCCOS(C)(=O)=O)CO[Si](C)(C)C(C)(C)C)COC1(C)C\",\n  \"functional_groups_formed\": [\"C-C double bonds\", \"carboxylic esters\"],\n  \"bonds_formed\": [\"6-6\", \"6-8\"],\n  \"bonds_broken\": [\"6-15\", \"6-6\", \"6-8\"],\n  \"limit\": 20\n}\n</action_input>": 0.0,
          "<thought>\nGood, I can see the available functional groups. Now let me try a different approach. Let me search for templates that form C-C double bonds and carboxylic esters without specifying a particular molecule, or try with a simpler search.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the task. The task from make_5_lvl2-apply_template-4 asked for \"all possible precursors of applying the template as the result of the task make_5_lvl2-template_search-4\". This suggests there was a previous template search (task 4) that found a template, and that template was applied to get these precursors.\n\nSo the current task (task 5) is asking me to find another template - one that reproduces the Still-Gennari reaction. Let me search more broadly for templates related to the Still-Gennari reaction characteristics.\n\nLet me try searching with just \"C-C double bonds\" formed:\n</thought>\n\n<action>search_template_catalog_by_criteria</action>\n<action_input>\n{\n  \"molecule_smiles\": \"CC(C)(C)OC(=O)N1[C@@H](C[C@@H](CCCOS(C)(=O)=O)CO[Si](C)(C)C(C)(C)C)COC1(C)C\",\n  \"functional_groups_formed\": [\"C-C double bonds\"],\n  \"limit\": 50\n}\n</action_input>": 0.0,
          "<thought>\nThe search returned no results. This might be because:\n1. The molecule I used might not be the correct target molecule\n2. The search criteria might be too specific\n3. The bonds specification might not match exactly\n\nLet me try a broader search with just the functional groups criteria, without specifying the exact bonds.\n</thought>\n\n<action>search_template_catalog_by_criteria</action>\n<action_input>\n{\n  \"molecule_smiles\": \"CC(C)(C)OC(=O)N1[C@@H](C[C@@H](CCCOS(C)(=O)=O)CO[Si](C)(C)C(C)(C)C)COC1(C)C\",\n  \"functional_groups_formed\": [\"C-C double bonds\", \"carboxylic esters\"],\n  \"limit\": 50\n}\n</action_input>": 0.0
